SUMMARY (not a substitute for the terms below, but it is what they mean)

  YOU MAY, freely and commercially, with no agreement to sign and no fee:
    - run QNet nodes of any type and earn network rewards;
    - serve RPC/API/WebSocket endpoints from your nodes, publicly, free or paid;
    - run explorers, faucets, dashboards, indexers, bridges and bots;
    - write, deploy and operate smart contracts, tokens and applications;
    - use it inside your company, and study or security-test it.

  YOU MAY NOT:
    - use this code to launch a blockchain network other than QNet;
    - sell "we host your node" as a product built on this code
      (running your own nodes and serving them publicly is fine);
    - ship modified copies of this software as a replacement for it;
    - strip the notices.

  If you are running nodes or building on QNet, everything you need is already
  granted. The restrictions exist to stop the network being cloned, not to stop
  it being used.


